        "new_text": "def filter_api_calls(\n    logp_with_result: np.ndarray,\n    logp_call_only: np.ndarray,\n    logp_no_call: np.ndarray,\n    tau_filter: float,\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Return an ordered keep mask and one finite margin per proposed call.\"\"\"\n    # Input validation\n    if not isinstance(tau_filter, (int, float)) or isinstance(tau_filter, bool):\n        raise ValueError(\"tau_filter must be a finite nonnegative number, not a boolean\")\n    if not np.isfinite(tau_filter) or tau_filter < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"tau_filter must be finite and nonnegative\")\n    for name, arr in [(\"logp_with_result\", logp_with_result), (\"logp_call_only\", logp_call_only), (\"logp_no_call\", logp_no_call)]:\n        if not isinstance(arr, np.ndarray) or arr.ndim != 2:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be a 2D numpy array\")\n        if arr.size == 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} is empty\")\n        if not np.isfinite(arr).all():\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} contains nonfinite values\")\n        if (arr > 0).any():\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} contains positive values\")\n    if not (logp_with_result.shape == logp_call_only.shape == logp_no_call.shape):\n        raise ValueError(\"All input arrays must have the same shape\")\n    # Compute total log probabilities over the future horizon\n    total_with = np.sum(logp_with_result, axis=1)\n    total_call = np.sum(logp_call_only, axis=1)\n    total_no = np.sum(logp_no_call, axis=1)\n    # Compute margin as logp_with_result advantage over best alternative\n    margins = total_with - np.maximum(total_call, total_no)\n    keep = margins > tau_filter\n    return keep, margins"
